In article <UZO=ekG00WB5ITrUtZ@andrew.cmu.edu> dh07+@andrew.cmu.edu (David Hairston) writes:
>credit cards have always seemed to be an anomoly since they don't do
>the obvious. with keys and lock picks abounding, credit cards ought to
>be given a more appropriate meaning ... 

I had seriously suggested that credit cards be replaced by ATM cards.  ATM
cards could be used at automatic teller machines, which have the mimic symbol
], and which would usually be found in shops, but occasionally outside.  You
could deposit or withdraw money as long as you had your card, and money
deposited in it could not be stolen and would not increase your inventory
weight.  Money-carrying monsters could also deposit their money in them (lost
forever to player).  Trying to put an ATM card in a mimic would just result in
the mimic eating both your card and any money you tried to deposit.

It was pointed out to me that an ATM already existed in Omega, and we didn't
want it to look like Nethack was just trying to copy it....
